      "retrieved": "2026-10-12",
      "revision": 1308769724,
      "text": "Sapindus rarak is a species of soapberry. It is a deciduous tree up to 42 metres (138 ft) tall native to south and east Asia. Its species name is derived from the Malaysian name rerak or rerek. In Indonesia it is commonly known as lerak or klerek."
